<blockquote><p>
A clergyman once asked Mr. Garrick, why a church congregation was seldom brought to tears, when the same persons placed in a theatre would be worked up to grief by a fictitious distress. &#8216;The reason,&#8217; answered Garrick, &#8216;is obvious; we repeat a <em>fiction</em> as though it were a <em>truth</em>; you repeat a <em>truth</em> as though it were a <em>fiction</em>.&#8217;
</p></blockquote>
